                    <coordinates>-104.8954657,39.7210515,0.0</coordinates>
                </Point>
            </Placemark>
            <Placemark id="885">
                <name>Clyfford Still Museum </name>
                <description>
                category  : See_Museums and architecture &lt;br&gt;
                address  : 1250 Bannock Street  &lt;br&gt;
                url  : https://clyffordstillmuseum.org/  &lt;br&gt;
                description  : Clyfford Still was in the first generation of US abstract expressionist artist of the early-mid 20th century. He pioneered the path which Rothko, Pollock, and others followed. But Still was not concerned with fame or sales, which is why you have heard of the others but not Still. And so he kept most of his works, and his will called for a city to create a museum to exhibit the whole collection, intact, which was a very Still move. Denver rose to the challenge, and the result is this museum: fascinating architecture with fascinating contents. The curators are interested not just in Still's work but in the questions it raises, such as how to preserve forever drawings which fade with light and paintings which darken with time. &lt;br&gt;
                </description>
                <styleUrl>#121</styleUrl>
                <Point id="884">
                    <coordinates>-104.98992,39.73645,0.0</coordinates>
                </Point>
            </Placemark>
            <Placemark id="887">
                <name>City Park </name>
                <description>
                category  : See_Parks and gardens &lt;br&gt;
                address  :   &lt;br&gt;
                url  :   &lt;br&gt;
                description  : Enjoy the Denver sunshine at this 330-acre urban park east of downtown. Two lakes, numerous fields, playgrounds, and a golf course, as well as the Denver Zoo and the Museum of Nature and Science are all within its expansive bounds. &lt;br&gt;
                </description>
                <styleUrl>#113</styleUrl>
                <Point id="886">
                    <coordinates>-104.9501,39.7477,0.0</coordinates>
                </Point>
            </Placemark>
            <Placemark id="889">
                <name>Denver Botanic Gardens </name>
                <description>
                category  : See_Parks and gardens &lt;br&gt;
                address  : 1005 York St  &lt;br&gt;
                url  : http://www.botanicgardens.org  &lt;br&gt;
                description  : Come for the array of flowers and plants from around the world, stay for the peace and quiet (and the free WiFi), then check out the bonus attractions. Above the gardens' bistro, you'll find Denver's first public green roof, a living example of the benefits of green design. Space and science buffs won't want to miss the OmniGlobe exhibit, a spherical simulation of the Earth from space. &lt;br&gt;
                </description>
                <styleUrl>#113</styleUrl>
                <Point id="888">
                    <coordinates>-104.960833,39.7325,0.0</coordinates>
                </Point>
            </Placemark>
            <Placemark id="891">
                <name>Washington Park </name>
                <description>
                category  : See_Parks and gardens &lt;br&gt;
                address  : S Downing St and E Louisiana Ave  &lt;br&gt;
                url  : https://www.denver.org/listing/washington-park/6828/  &lt;br&gt;
                description  : Beautiful and lush Denver park, with lakes, flower gardens, a recreation center, soccer fields and tennis courts. Over 160 acres of natural beauty, surrounded by turn-of-the-19th-century homes. A favorite jogging, volleyball, and drinking destination. This used to be the favorite hang-out of young residents during the summer months, but regulations requiring permits for many common activities have reduced park usage and transferred it to City Park. &lt;br&gt;
                </description>
                <styleUrl>#113</styleUrl>
                <Point id="890">
                    <coordinates>-104.971,39.7,0.0</coordinates>
