            <Placemark id="1117">
                <name>Acoma House </name>
                <description>
                category  : Sleep_Mid-range &lt;br&gt;
                address  : 1114 Acoma Street  &lt;br&gt;
                url  : https://www.theacomahouse.com/  &lt;br&gt;
                description  : This small colourful hotel features 24 rooms, each painted in vivid colours designed by a different artist. A wide range of amenities for the modern traveller, including fast internet, free water and coffee pods, a tiny kitchen in each room, and laundry machines downstairs. There is no lobby or reception desk. You check in with a door code which they text to you the day before you check in. No elevator, so rooms 201-212 require you to carry luggage up narrow stairs, but ground floor rooms 101-112 are accessible by a ramp at the rear of the building. Downstairs is free luggage storage, a lounge, and a meeting room. Parking $11/day by arrangement with the lot next to the hotel. Easy walking to the civic center and a few local shops, restaurants, and museums. E-scooters are plentiful nearby, and bring most of downtown in range. &lt;br&gt;
                </description>
                <styleUrl>#101</styleUrl>
